     <td>PINNACLE</td>\n                <td>₦1,635.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DUPORT</td>\n                <td>₦1,650.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AFRICAN TERMINAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,650.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBETO</td>\n                <td>₦1,650.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DANGOTE</td>\n                <td>₦1,608.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>RAINOIL LAGOS</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>A.Y.M SHAFA</td>\n                <td>₦1,720.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>FYNEFIELD</td>\n                <td>₦1,700.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Calabar Petrol Price War Intensifies as Depot Prices Near Lagos Levels\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Petrol prices in Calabar are coming under increasing pressure as competing marketers push depot prices lower. This has narrowed the gap with Lagos, Nigeria’s traditional low-price hub for refined petroleum products.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/calabar-petrol-price-war-intensifies-as-depot-prices-near-lagos-levels\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Tinubu Vows to Revive Nigeria's Refineries, Promises Structural Reset\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    President Bola Tinubu has assured that Nigeria's refineries will be revived and repositioned to become profitable. The President gave the assurance on Thursday when he received the newly elected national executive of the Nigerian Union of Petroleum and Natural Gas Workers (NUPENG) He added that a refinery producing flame and smoke does not necessarily mean it is functional.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/tinubu-vows-to-revive-nigerias-refineries-promises-structural-reset\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Dangote Refinery to List IPO in Nigeria Before Any Foreign Debut — David Bird\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Dangote Petroleum Refinery is concentrating on its planned Nigerian stock market debut. Any move to an international exchange unlikely for at least three years, according to Chief Executive Officer David Bird. The position comes as the refinery prepares for a potential $5 billion initial public offering in Nigeria.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/dangote-refinery-to-list-ipo-in-nigeria-before-any-foreign-debut-david-bird\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Strait of Hormuz Oil Flows Under Pressure as Tanker Traffic Falls\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Tanker movements through the Strait of Hormuz have dropped sharply as the US-Iran standoff shows no clear sign of ending. Only five tanker crossings were recorded on Wednesday and nine on Thursday, compared with a monthly average of 12 crossings.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/strait-of-hormuz-oil-flows-under-pressure-as-tanker-traffic-falls\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Strait of Hormuz Crisis: 94 Countries Turn to Fuel Subsidies as Nigerians Pay More\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria is facing renewed pressure from the global energy shock. Governments in 94 countries introduce fuel subsidies, price caps and tax measures to shield consumers from soaring energy costs. The International Energy Agency said more than 115 countries had introduced measures in response to the crisis.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/strait-of-hormuz-crisis-94-countries-turn-to-fuel-subsidies-as-nigerians-pay-more\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
